x86_64-windows  a class is neither thrown nor caught on this target yet - `catch (std::bad_alloc &)` is refused by name, the Microsoft ThrowInfo chain for a class being its own step - so the runtime's bad_alloc cannot be caught here. The half that needs no exception, `new (std::nothrow)` and the new handler, is new-nothrow.cpp and runs on this target.
tms6747  the emulator's runtime has no `std::set_new_handler`, no nothrow `operator new` and no `std::bad_alloc` - `<new>` declares them as TI's rts6740 exports them, and the emulator answers "undefined symbol" at the first. A program that uses none of them, placement-array-new.cpp, runs here.
